{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_24\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 24</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_24\">Problem 24</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 24\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the value of the following limit?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/475137028e9e078545947c5453f165d5c88f62b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim_{x \\to 5} \\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{x}-\\sqrt[3]{5}}{x-5}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/387ef157c9d1672ab23336c0b43159784c5c5b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\dfrac{\\ln 5}{15}  \\quad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{5\\sqrt[3]{5}}  \\quad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{9}  \\quad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3 \\sqrt[3]{25}}  \\quad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{The limit does not exist}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"543\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Seeing the cube roots in the numerator, we notice that the the denominator is a difference of cubes with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5cb65218fd2c64fcae3654a0fc061916e84d215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\sqrt[3]{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb41eea17136c35e62c63e657283cc9c3133f97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\sqrt[3]{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"21\" />, which can be factorized:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f0a256ac34c0d434e2d34df1abb55cba027e9a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{x}-\\sqrt[3]{5}}{x-5} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{x}-\\sqrt[3]{5}}{\\left(\\sqrt[3]{x} - \\sqrt[3]{5}\\right)\\left(\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}} + \\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt[3]{5} + \\sqrt[3]{5^{2}}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}} + \\sqrt[3]{x}\\sqrt[3]{5} + \\sqrt[3]{5^{2}}}\\]\" width=\"571\" height=\"58\" />\nNow, we can plug <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> in to obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/8/548f7f9803e640d5c678f7b8f817a068cbee77be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim_{x \\to 5} \\dfrac{\\sqrt[3]{x}-\\sqrt[3]{5}}{x-5} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{5^{2}} + \\sqrt[3]{5}\\sqrt[3]{5} + \\sqrt[3]{5^{2}}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3 \\sqrt[3]{25}}}.\\]\" width=\"415\" height=\"52\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c80ea5862b45877f08d698a0c893bd2806a2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> in the numerator and denominator, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/6/9660a8de7fa5633368aac9236c785a6804810ef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{5} - \\sqrt[3]{5} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/a/ada6c233c82ad86c6f9a94d13179aa766e42989a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 - 5 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, so this is the indeterminate form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d7ada08ad200c068f7060c22ead4ad2e1a2e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{0}{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. Thus, we can use L'Hopital's rule and differentiate the numerator and denominator:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d9cff4a61ce31b8f24113368b62162a7186388.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lim_{x \\to 5} \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{x}-\\sqrt[3]{5}}{x-5} = \\lim_{x \\to 5} \\frac{ \\frac{d}{dx} \\left[ \\sqrt[3]{x} - \\sqrt[3]{5} \\right] }{ \\frac{d}{dx} \\left[ x-5 \\right] } = \\lim_{x \\to 5} \\frac{ \\frac{1}{3}x^{-\\frac{2}{3}} }{1} = \\frac{1}{3} (5)^{-\\frac{2}{3}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3 \\sqrt[3]{25}}}\\]\" width=\"577\" height=\"62\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We recognize this as the limit definition of a derivative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/e/e6ecd17560a11991ee45d0c497b46285ad7141c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lim\\limits_{x \\to c} \\frac{ f(x) - f(c) }{ x - c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"126\" height=\"42\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/eda98cca3591121f041ec3d26a4aad8cc82dfe78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\sqrt[3]{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"22\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb45ac08f0a40da167c4e3ade6cb5639057bcc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = 5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, we calculate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/7/2875ce128e60120eba7b8d8c634ec9fffcdaccc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x) = \\frac{1}{3}x^{-2/3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d6758e3a57306eff2e6e5bb6981c048d376f4785.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(5) = \\frac{1}{3}(5)^{-\\frac{2}{3}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\dfrac{1}{3 \\sqrt[3]{25}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"240\" height=\"54\" />.\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_